  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "Main set-up: UNO programmer (uno2) to UNO target (uno1) with the 'old style' wiring: D11-D11 (MOSI), D12-D12 (MISO), D13-D13 (SCK), programmer D10 to target RESET, 5V-5V, GND-GND. The ICSP header is not in the catalogue, so the digital-pin option from the manual's table is used.",
   "The LED circuit follows the ArduinoISP sketch pins: heartbeat on D9, error on D8, programming on D7. Each runs pin -> 220 ohm resistor -> LED anode, with the cathode on the breadboard ground rail (tn). The ground rail is fed from programmer GND.2.",
   "The manual gives no resistor value, LED colours or breadboard hole positions, so the 220 ohm value and the hole positions are assumptions.",
   "The 10 \u00b5F capacitor sits on the programmer: positive to programmer RESET through wire11 and the breadboard, negative to the ground rail. The manual says to add it only after the ArduinoISP sketch is uploaded.",
   "The USB cable and computer are not modelled, because the manual says not to connect USB or power while wiring."
  ]
 },
